  "note": "Current post-2025 yellow ochre façade and five statues are confirmed in both comparison exteriors; the former white/statue-free Commons views were rejected. Parish history confirms the 2022–2025 statue restoration and quotes 45 ×33 ×20 m, whereas OSM measures about49.9 ×23.3 m including the rear sacristy. Height is an unsurveyed 27m photo/footprint estimate to the cross, with nave pediment20.2m and porch13.5m: the published20m may exclude the lantern and is not treated as a surveyed overall height. Only the mapped main church/rear sacristy are owned; the detached modern bell frame and plaza fountain are excluded. Porch floor/steps begin above local grade; no plaza or terrain is authored. Geographic yaw baked once from mapped controls [[55.4486105, -20.8772813], [55.4490273, -20.8771913]]. Cityscape: not tested; Full 3D world: not tested.",
